      "content": "thanks for this. the tone is okay but i'm worried the marketing team won't be impressed with the score. they're pretty strict about the \"feature-rich\" metric and might flag it if the count of unique features doesn't hit the maximum. \n\nit's fine if it's a bit dense, as long as it still feels professional. can u rewrite it to make sure all 20 features from the list are actually in the text? just try to get that score as high as possible.",
